.TH SPIRULA-STUDIO 1 "November 2026" "Spirula Studio"
.SH NAME
spirula-studio \- create and view 3D models from photos or video
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spirula-studio
.RI [ options ] " [files]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vulkan is the default backend. Use the desktop CUDA action or put
.B --compute-backend=cuda
first to select the separately installed CUDA backend.
The Graphics page chooses the GPU by stable identity for training,
structure from motion and model inference.
The native program prints its active backend and GPU.
.SH STEREO
Enable 3D, render resolution per eye, and Display Settings are the
three stereo controls. Stereo KWin supplies the depth limits.
Missing limits produce identical eyes with an explicit message.
.SH PROCESSING DATA
Model profiles are separate packages. Their installation displays
the pinned publisher, current download size, metered notice and terms.
Required consent is never assumed. Missing profiles open their
AppCenter installation page; the application never downloads them.
Installer-owned models are under /var/lib/spirula-studio/models.
Removing a package keeps them. Purging a profile deletes its unshared
files. Purging spirula-studio deletes all its installer-owned models.
The person's other files are kept.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sparky-install-models (1)
